</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>SD = standard deviation</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>The total numbers of of hypoechogeneic and hyperechogeneic lesions at different anatomical sites in the three groups of horses studied.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left"><bold>Groups</bold></td><td align="center" colspan="2"><bold>Interspinous space</bold></td><td align="center" colspan="2"><bold>Above DSP</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Total</bold></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan="4"><hr></hr></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center"><bold>Hypoechoic</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Hyperechoic</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Hypoechoic</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Hyperechoic</bold></td><td></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left"><bold>G1(Unridden)</bold></td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">33</td><td align="center">25</td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">64</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>G2 (No pain)</bold></td><td align="center">14</td><td align="center">17</td><td align="center">7</td><td align="center">0</td><td align="center">38</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>G3 (Pain)</bold></td><td align="center">10</td><td align="center">19</td><td align="center">30</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">61</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>Total</bold></td><td align="center">30</td><td align="center">69</td><td align="center">62</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">163</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></sec></back></article>